From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:30:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] UefiPayloadPkg/FmpDeviceSmmLib: Update one vboot slot at a
 time

A firmware verified by vboot with two RW slots is updated with a
capsule whose manifest names both, RW_SECTION_A and RW_SECTION_B.
Writing both, as the manifest says, leaves nothing to boot from if the
update is cut short.

With such a manifest, read the nvdata of vboot from RW_NVRAM (the
format of coreboot's vbnv_flash.c), write only the slot that vboot did
not boot, with the other regions of the manifest, and then append a
record that asks vboot to try that slot for two boots. If the write is
cut short, vboot still boots the old slot; if the new slot does not
verify, vboot goes back to the old one; if it does not boot far enough
to report it (SMMSTORE_CMD_VBOOT_SLOT_GOOD), vboot goes back once the
tries run out. A full RW_NVRAM is erased first, which needs it to be
whole flash blocks; otherwise the capsule is refused before anything is
written.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
